WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.364
Solve in C
Solve z squared minus two z plus five equal to zero. Here the unknown is a
complex number. We will work through an organized solution.

2
00:00:14.364 --> 00:00:29.182
Identify the coefficients
First identify the coefficients. The coefficient of the square is one, that of
z is minus two, and the constant is five. Now calculate the discriminant.

3
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:44.000
Calculate the discriminant
The discriminant is b squared minus four a c. Here it is four minus twenty, or
minus sixteen. Its negative value leads to nonreal complex solutions.

4
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:58.364
First complex root
The square root of minus delta is four. The first solution is two plus four i,
divided by two. Divide both numerator terms by two.

5
00:00:58.364 --> 00:01:14.545
Second complex root
For the second solution, change the sign of the imaginary part. Two minus four
i divided by two gives one minus two i, the conjugate of the first root.

6
00:01:14.545 --> 00:01:29.818
Check the sum and product
The solutions are conjugates. Check that their sum is two and their product is
five, as required by the equation. This verifies the calculation before moving
on.
